  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "2 v 1 – the keeper picks",
  "description": "Three lines stand side by side a little way out from the goal, about 20 metres wide and 20–25 metres deep. The keeper starts by passing or throwing to one of the outside lines. The other outside player, who did not get the ball, becomes the defender. The other two attack and try to get a shot off 2 v 1 as quickly as possible.\n\nIf the defender wins the ball, they counter towards one of the two small goals behind the lines, and the attackers work to win it back. Offside applies. Switch lines after each go. Vary it with the keeper kicking the ball out in the air.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The player on the ball attacks the defender at speed, so the defender has to commit."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The player without the ball makes a run that gives an option: a wall pass, an overlap or a run in behind."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pick the option from what the defender does – pass when they come at you, dribble when they wait."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Keep the tempo and finish quickly before the defence gets back."
    }
  ],
